  "steps": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "text": "Heat the oil in the skillet over medium. Add the mustard seeds and cover at once — they pop hard. Once the popping calms (about 15 seconds), add the cumin seeds."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "text": "Add the shallots, green chili, and curry leaves; cook 3 minutes, stirring, until the shallots soften and pick up color. Timer: 3 minutes.",
      "timer_min": 3
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "text": "Add the cabbage with the turmeric and salt; toss so the shreds turn faintly yellow all over."
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "text": "Cover and cook on medium-low about 8 minutes, tossing twice — the cabbage wilts in its own moisture and no water is needed. Timer: 8 minutes.",
      "timer_min": 8
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "text": "Uncover, raise the heat, and cook 1 minute so the last of the liquid steams off; the pan should stay dry-ish.",
      "timer_min": 1
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "text": "Off the heat, fold in the grated coconut so it warms through without frying — it should stay snow-white against the yellow cabbage."
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "text": "Taste for salt and serve alongside rice and any curry; it travels well in a lunch box too."
    }
  ],
